What:		/sys/devices/platform/11005000.serial/sleep_state
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	FuQuan <i@fuquan.moe>
Description:
		Read-only cached MT6580 UART system-sleep handshake snapshots.
		Available on enabled MT6580 UART controller devices, including
		11006000.serial when enabled. No UART register reads are performed
		by this attribute. prepared means the temporary register-clock
		references are held for a sleep request. requests counts accepted
		sleep acknowledgments, restores counts completed request/control
		restoration, and skips counts live-console/wakeup-tty bypasses.
		error records the last suspend handshake or wake restoration errno.
		saved_en/saved_req are the original controls; sleep_ack/wake_ack
		are the acknowledgment snapshots after request and restoration.
		context saves/restores count native-field snapshots and completed
		restores. changed_fields counts fields differing before restoration,
		and errors counts failed readback checks. saved/before/restored show
		GUARD (0x3c), RX_SEL (0xb0), RATE_FIX (0x34), respectively. These
		fields are not rebuilt by serial core or MTK set_termios; changed
		values are restored before completing the wake handshake. Standard
		8250, FIFO, EFR and baud state remain owned by the serial core.
		The handshake does not by itself turn off the UART or system clocks.
